            <ArticleTitle>Interaction prediction in structure-based virtual screening using deep learning.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0010-4825(17)30297-4</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.compbiomed.2017.09.007</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We introduce a deep learning architecture for structure-based virtual screening that generates fixed-sized fingerprints of proteins and small molecules by applying learnable atom convolution and softmax operations to each molecule separately. These fingerprints are further non-linearly transformed, their inner product is calculated and used to predict the binding potential. Moreover, we show that widely used benchmark datasets may be insufficient for testing structure-based virtual screening methods that utilize machine learning. Therefore, we introduce a new benchmark dataset, which we constructed based on DUD-E, MUV and PDBBind databases.</AbstractText>
